  "title": "Building a Safe Parenting Mindset",
  "content": "A safe parenting mindset is built on self‑reflection, emotional awareness, and the willingness to grow. Parenting is not about being perfect; it is about being present, learning from mistakes, and repairing when things go wrong. Children benefit most from parents who can acknowledge their own emotions and take responsibility for their behaviour.\n\nThis lesson helps parents understand how mindset influences daily interactions. When parents shift from reacting to responding, they create a calmer environment. When they shift from control to connection, children become more cooperative.\n\nWe explore how to build a mindset that supports long‑term change, resilience, and emotional safety.",
  "activities": [
    "Write down one belief about parenting you want to let go of and one belief you want to strengthen.",
    "Practice a repair conversation with your child after a moment of tension."
  ],
  "reflectionQuestions": [
    "What mindset do you want to bring into your parenting?",
    "How do you want your child to feel when they are around you?",
    "What does ‘safe parenting’ mean to you personally?"
